16556	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s3","entry":{"id":"review-9a487082b2bab10eeff6b3e89c83536e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:44:26.188Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's acceptance-criteria mapping (ac1-ac5, §7) reproduces exactly the s3 acceptance criteria approved in the DEF (grouped on-demand investigation, bounded continuation/yield, retry/pause without draining backlog, read-only/serial/trust boundary, and stale/missing index-impact disclosure).","evidence":"DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json s3.acceptanceCriteria ac1..ac5 (lines ~303-353) state: 'both review modes choose necessary packet blocks...may assess related obligations together, without mandatory eager chunking or one call per clause' (ac1); 'yields an explicit continuation with coverage and pending work...does not truncate required evidence or claim completion' (ac2); 'remaining work is paused with a typed reason...retries are bounded' (ac3); 'review operations remain read-only...LLM calls remain serial' (ac4); 'discloses index freshness and coverage limits...neither treats missing callers as proof of no impact nor widens the selected commit set' (ac5). These map 1:1 onto LLD §7's review-s3-ac1..ac5 test subjects and §3.2-3.4 prose. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Compared DEF acceptance criteria text against LLD §7 acceptance mapping table and §3 prose claims.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD does not build any of the Epic's declared non-goals (no severity-policy change/auto-approve, no new usage warehouse/model catalog/board UI, no recovery of never-persisted legacy answers, no replacement of design-document review).","evidence":"DEF nonGoals (lines 84-105) list exactly those five exclusions. LLD §3.4 explicitly says 'no new usage store or artifact JSON collection' and reuses sc6.recordAttemptUsage with existing counter fields; §1/§5 state s3 does not touch design-document review, approval, or CR publication. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Checked DEF nonGoals against LLD §3.4 usage-handling language and §1/§5 scope statements.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's claim that today's LLMProvider.runReviewSession / ReviewSessionOpts exposes no incremental progress/ACK bridge, only budget/cwd/deadline/retry/stall/signal, is accurate.","evidence":"src/shared/types.ts:243-263 defines `runReviewSession?<T>(prompt, schema, opts: ReviewSessionOpts)` and `ReviewSessionOpts` with only `reviewBudget`, `cwd`, `deadlineMs`, `internalRetry`, `stallMs`, `signal` fields — no per-block progress/read callback of any kind. [files: src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Read src/shared/types.ts around the ReviewSessionOpts/runReviewSession declarations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc1 (ReviewSubjectV1 family) and sc6 (ReviewRuntimePortsV1, ReviewReadReceiptV1, ReviewUsageObservationV1) that the LLD marks 'consumes' already exist with the exact shape cited in the HLD's interfaceSketch.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts:3-39 defines ReviewSubjectV1, CommitPacketV1, ReviewRuntimePortsV1 (readEvidence/stageImmutableValue/appendTransition/recordAttemptUsage), ReviewUsageObservationV1 and ReviewReadReceiptV1 verbatim-matching the HLD sc1/sc6 interfaceSketches and the LLD's §2/§3 signatures. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts and diffed field-for-field against HLD sc1/sc6 interfaceSketch and LLD contract blocks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc2 (EvidenceV1/CoverageV1/ReviewLedgerV1/LedgerBasis and admitLedgerEvidence/applyReviewLedgerDelta/validateReviewLedger) that the LLD reuses already exists with the stated shape, including the 'caller-impact' evidence kind and index-freshness metadata the LLD's impact-evidence design depends on.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger-types.ts:4-38 defines EvidenceV1 (with kind 'caller-impact', index-bearing TrustedInspectionReceipt) and CoverageV1/ReviewLedgerV1/LedgerBasis exactly as cited; ledger.ts:63-80 exports validateReviewLedger/applyReviewLedgerDelta, and ledger-evidence.ts:45-71 exports admitLedgerEvidence/evidenceFromReceipt enforcing index freshness/coverage rules for 'caller-impact' evidence that the LLD's §3.2 impact-evidence rules rely on. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger-types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger-evidence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger.ts]","action":"Read ledger-types.ts and ledger-evidence.ts and matched against LLD §2 CoverageV1 reuse and §3.2 impact-evidence admission rules.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The budget helpers (createReviewBudgetPolicy/measureReviewBudget) and the daemon-owned findCallers graph traversal that the LLD claims to reuse (not reimplement) already exist with usable signatures.","evidence":"src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts:86-148 exports createReviewBudgetPolicy and measureReviewBudget performing exactly the reserve/host/schema/tools-manifest admission math the LLD §3.4 describes reusing; src/daemon/tools/builtins/graph/index.ts:11,189 imports and dispatches findCallers/findCallees through a closure-scoped adapter, matching the LLD's 'inject a closure-scoped adapter; no DB handles in client/controller' claim. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/graph/index.ts]","action":"Read budget.ts and daemon/tools/builtins/graph/index.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed new files (investigation-types.ts, continuation.ts, progress.ts, continuation-policy.ts) and the InvestigationBackend/InvestigationTools seams do not already exist under any name in the investigation module, so classifying them 'new' (§3.1-§3.4) is correct and no existing caller/signature is silently being changed.","evidence":"Glob for src/workflow/code-review/investigation/{continuation,continuation-policy,progress,investigation-types}.ts returned no matches; the existing investigation/ directory only contains subject/source/ledger*/identity/work/git-packets files (listed via Glob), none of which declare InvestigationTurnV1, InvestigationReplyV1, ImpactCapabilityV1, ReviewBlockProgressV1 or BlockCheckpointReceiptV1. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/]","action":"Globbed for the LLD's proposed filenames and the investigation directory's existing file list; grepped for the proposed type names.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"LLMProvider/CliProvider/OllamaProvider/runReviewSession and ReadOnlyToolLoop signatures, which the LLD states stay unchanged in this Story, carry no pre-existing method whose signature this Story's new seams would collide with or silently widen.","evidence":"src/shared/types.ts's LLMProvider interface exposes only completeStructured/runReviewSession?/capabilities; src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts's ReadOnlyToolLoopArgs (lines 46-60) already carries reviewBudget/connectionExecution/allow fields the LLD's new coordinator is described as composing around, not replacing. [files: src/shared/types.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Read the LLMProvider interface and ReadOnlyToolLoopArgs to confirm no signature overlap with the LLD's new InvestigationBackend/InvestigationTools seam.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new BlockProgressTransitionV1 payload's explicit version:1 tag and reliance on s4 for storage/replay is consistent with the already-approved sc4 (ReviewRecoveryV1) schema, which itself declares schemaVersion:1 and an explicit migration/compatibility story — so s3 is not introducing an unversioned or migration-incompatible shape at the one boundary (sc6.stageImmutableValue) it touches.","evidence":"HLD sc4 interfaceSketch declares `interface ReviewRecoveryV1 { readonly schemaVersion: 1; ... }` and HLD body states 'A schema migration is explicit and tested; unsupported state stays readable as unsupported.' LLD §3.3's `BlockProgressTransitionV1 { readonly version: 1; ... }` and 'Same progressId + payloadDigest resolves the same accepted receipt from authoritative context' follow the identical versioning/idempotent-replay convention, and s3 itself owns no durable store (s4 does), so there are no 'older records' for s3 to migrate. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Compared HLD sc4 interfaceSketch/migration language against LLD §3.3's BlockProgressTransitionV1 versioning and s4/s3 ownership split in §1 and §8.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's 'Owns: sc3; Consumes: sc1, sc2, sc6' and its adjacent-scope table (s1/s2/s4/s5/s6 exclusions) match the approved HLD's storyBoundaries entry for s3 exactly, so s3 is not redesigning another Story's owned contract.","evidence":"HLD storyBoundaries s3 entry: `owns: [\"sc3\"], depends: [\"sc1\",\"sc2\",\"sc6\"]`, internal text: 'Own independent read-only task-directed continuation behavior... no durable storage implementation or terminal approval logic... External registration belongs to s6.' This is reproduced verbatim in the LLD's §1 'Adjacent scope' table for s1/s2/s4/s5/s6. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Compared HLD storyBoundaries[s3] (and the s1/s2/s4/s5/s6 entries it must not redesign) against LLD §1.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD honors the HLD's explicit prohibition that s3 must not acquire a 'forbidden backwards dependency on s4' (durable recovery) and must not register MCP phases owned by s6/S005, by keeping its backend/port interfaces type-level and in-memory only.","evidence":"HLD body 'AUTHOR CONSISTENCY NOTES': 's1 owns sc6's type-level persistence/usage ports; s4 implements them and s6 wires production, so s3 does not acquire a forbidden backwards dependency on s4.' LLD §3.1: 'In-memory ports and deterministic backend/provider fixtures are scaffolding, explicitly not production durability... s4 implements durable ports' and §8 Migration keeps 'production selection disabled until s4/s6 provide durable/qualified adapters.' [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Checked the HLD's backwards-dependency and MCP-ownership prohibitions against LLD §3.1 and §8 migration steps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed InvestigationError class (code + message, typed error codes) follows the same pattern already used by sibling error classes in this subsystem (ReviewLedgerError, ReviewRuntimePortError, SubjectPreparationError, ReviewBudgetError), so its detectability/handling design is realistic and consistent with how callers already branch on `.code`.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts:76-84 defines `ReviewRuntimePortError`/`SubjectPreparationError` as `class X extends Error { constructor(readonly code: ..., message: string) {...} }`; src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger-types.ts:68-72 defines `ReviewLedgerError` identically; src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts:19-30 defines `ReviewBudgetError` the same way. The LLD's §6 error cases (unsupported-backend, invalid-progress, budget-refused, etc.) are designed to surface through an `InvestigationError` of the same shape. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/ledger-types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts]","action":"Read the existing error classes in investigation/types.ts, ledger-types.ts and budget.ts and compared their code/message/catch-site convention to the LLD's §6 error-path design.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cancellation via AbortSignal, which the LLD's error paths rely on for budget/time exhaustion and user cancellation, is already a first-class, honored input on the exact session boundary (ReviewSessionOpts.signal) the new coordinator composes around.","evidence":"src/shared/types.ts:262 `readonly signal?: AbortSignal | undefined; /** Cancels the session. */` on ReviewSessionOpts — the same signal type the LLD's §3.4 'Abort propagates to provider and tools' and InvestigationTools.execute(turn, tools, signal: AbortSignal) rely on. [files: src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Re-examined ReviewSessionOpts.signal in src/shared/types.ts against the LLD's execute() signature and §6 cancellation error case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each DEF acceptance criterion ac1-ac5 for s3 maps to a named test in the LLD's §7 acceptance-mapping table, satisfying the per-criterion test-mapping requirement, and the referenced fixture/test style (deterministic backend, fake clock, in-memory ports) matches the already-established pattern in the sibling s1/s2 investigation tests this Story is said to follow.","evidence":"LLD §7 'Acceptance mapping' table binds ac1..ac5 each to at least one named test (e.g. ac1->'review-s3-ac1 grouped investigation', ac5->'review-s3-ac5 index/entity limits'), matching DEF's s3.acceptanceCriteria ac1..ac5 one-for-one. The existing investigation/__tests__ directory already contains ledger-fixtures.ts, adversarial.test.ts, source.test.ts, git-packets.test.ts etc., confirming the deterministic-fixture/no-live-model-suite convention the LLD's Test framework line claims to continue. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Cross-checked LLD §7 acceptance-mapping rows against DEF s3 ac1-ac5 ids, and listed the existing investigation/__tests__ directory to confirm the deterministic-fixture convention referenced as precedent.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No acceptance criterion is left without a mapped test, and no test subject claims coverage of functionality outside this Story's owned sc3 contract (e.g. no test claims to validate sc4 durability or sc5/sc6 publication, which the design correctly defers).","evidence":"LLD §7's integration subjects explicitly note 'durable restart is s4 test obligation' and 'no MCP registration, legacy/provider signature changes or production activation' — the test list stays within sc3's domain scope rather than asserting coverage the Story does not own.","action":"Read the LLD §7 integration-level test subjects and fixtures list for scope leakage into s4/s5/s6 responsibilities.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-29T06:44:26.188Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
